<Ui>
    <!--
        The two bottom multibars (vanilla MultiBarBottomLeft / MultiBarBottomRight), ALWAYS ON —
        the director's call: no interface-options toggles, no SHOW_MULTI_ACTIONBAR_* state, no
        CMSG_SET_ACTION_BAR_TOGGLES roaming (the server-side PLAYER_FIELD_BYTES byte the real
        options screen persists is ignored entirely).

        Geometry + slot ranges QUOTED from the real 1.12 FrameXML (extracted from patch.MPQ):
        - ref-MultiActionBars.xml l.36-39/496-513: each bar a 500x38 frame; BottomLeft's
          BOTTOMLEFT anchors to ActionButton1's TOPLEFT +(0,17); BottomRight's LEFT anchors to
          BottomLeft's RIGHT +(10,0); 12 buttons chained BOTTOMLEFT then LEFT-of-prev-RIGHT +6.
        - ref-ActionButton.lua l.6-9/446-467 (ActionButton_GetPagedID): BottomLeft = page 6 ⇒
          actions 61..72; BottomRight = page 5 ⇒ actions 49..60. The bases below feed
          BenillaActionButton_Action (ActionBar.xml), which carries the ref's parent-name fork
          as per-button data.
        - Buttons reuse BenillaActionButtonTemplate + the whole ActionBar.xml handler set: same
          click/drag/keyless-use, same feedback layer (state/usable/cooldown/flash), fanned from
          MainMenuBar's bar-level events via the BENILLA_ACTION_BUTTONS roster each button
          joins at OnLoad.

        Ref divergences (deliberate, mirroring ActionBar.xml's SCOPE notes):
        - MULTIACTIONBAR1/2BUTTON1-12 are BINDABLE since 1008 (the ref's own commands, registered
          in crate::bindings::commands with the ref's runOnUp pair below); they ship UNBOUND like
          the ref (no MULTIACTIONBAR* line in any of the install's bindings-cache.wtf files), so
          out of the box the hotkey corner still carries the ref's range dot — a bound slot wears
          its abbreviated label exactly like the main bar (ActionBar.xml's PaintHotkey law).
        - Empty wells hide (the ref's own default) and appear as drop-target rings only while a
          cursor payload is held — unlike the main bar's always-visible wells (its art has
          sockets; floating rings over bare world would not read as a bar).
        - The vertical MultiBarRight/MultiBarLeft (pages 3/4, actions 25..48) stay OUT — only the
          two bottom bars were asked for; the base-as-data mechanism extends to them for free.
    -->
    <Script><![CDATA[
        -- ref ActionButton.lua:6-7 — BOTTOMLEFT_ACTIONBAR_PAGE = 6, BOTTOMRIGHT_ACTIONBAR_PAGE = 5;
        -- base = (page - 1) * 12.
        BENILLA_MULTIBAR_BOTTOMLEFT_BASE = 60
        BENILLA_MULTIBAR_BOTTOMRIGHT_BASE = 48
        -- ref ActionButton.lua:8-9 — LEFT_ACTIONBAR_PAGE = 4, RIGHT_ACTIONBAR_PAGE = 3.
        BENILLA_MULTIBAR_LEFT_BASE = 36
        BENILLA_MULTIBAR_RIGHT_BASE = 24

        -- The MULTIACTIONBAR keybind pair — ref MultiActionBars.lua:24-45 MultiActionButtonDown/Up,
        -- the same NORMAL→PUSHED debounce dance as the main bar's ActionButtonDown/Up
        -- (ActionBar.xml — the ref's MacroFrame_SaveMacro hook is not modeled there either).
        -- Driven by the binding dispatch (crate::bindings, Kind::EdgeUpDown — decision 1008).
        --
        -- `bar` IS THE WHOLE FRAME-NAME PREFIX, not a suffix (decision 1199). The reference resolves
        -- `getglobal(bar.."Button"..id)` and its own Bindings.xml passes "MultiBarBottomLeft"; ours
        -- used to pass "BottomLeft" and splice "MultiBar" on in here. Same arity, different MEANING
        -- — the silent kind of wrong shape: zBar calls `MultiActionButtonDown("zBar"..barid, id)`
        -- and under the old splice built the nonexistent frame name "MultiBarzBar1Button1". The
        -- caller now names the bar in full, exactly as the reference's binding does, so a third-
        -- party bar can address these at all. `onSelf` rides to UseAction like ActionButtonUp's.
        function MultiActionButtonDown(bar, id)
            local button = getglobal(bar .. "Button" .. id)
            if ( button:GetButtonState() == "NORMAL" ) then
                button:SetButtonState("PUSHED")
            end
        end

        function MultiActionButtonUp(bar, id, onSelf)
            local button = getglobal(bar .. "Button" .. id)
            if ( button:GetButtonState() == "PUSHED" ) then
                button:SetButtonState("NORMAL")
                UseAction(BenillaActionButton_Action(button), 0, onSelf)
                -- Ref MultiActionButtonUp:39-43: the checked ring reflects the use immediately.
                BenillaActionButton_UpdateState(button)
            end
        end
    ]]></Script>

