    <!-- **The two VERTICAL bars, built but never shown.**

         They were scoped out (see the header's ref-divergence note) on the reasonable reading that
         a bar nobody asked for should not exist. Measuring the corpus corrected the reading: the
         reference does not choose between "shown" and "absent" — `MultiActionBars.xml` l.515/523
         instantiates BOTH as real `parent="UIParent"` frames whose templates (VerticalMultiBar3/4,
         l.266/381) carry `hidden="true"`. On the real client they exist from load and stay hidden
         until SHOW_MULTI_ACTIONBAR_3/4. So declaring them costs nothing on screen and is what the
         reference actually does.

         What it buys: Atlas, Bartender2 and FuBartender2 all DIE at session start on
         `MultiBarLeft` — Atlas at `Atlas.lua:387` (`MultiBarLeft:SetFrameStrata("MEDIUM")`),
         Bartender2 at `Bartender2.lua:74` (`MultiBarLeft:ClearAllPoints()`). Neither shows the bar;
         both only need it to be there. Five more addons index `MultiBarRight` (decision 1218's
         corrected ranking).

         Still no SHOW_MULTI_ACTIONBAR_* state and still no options toggle — 0270's call stands, and
         these two are simply hidden rather than optional. An addon that calls `MultiBarLeft:Show()`
         gets a working bar on actions 37..48, which is exactly what the reference gives it.

         The buttons carry the reference's own MULTIACTIONBAR3/4BUTTON command names, and those
         commands stay OUT of `bindings::commands` — 1008's "honest tree" holds: the keybind screen
         lists what the player can actually reach, and a bar we never show is not that. Painting a
         hotkey from an unregistered command is a no-op (GetBindingKey answers nil), so the label is
         simply blank until someone registers them.

         Pages from ref-ActionButton.lua l.8-9: LEFT_ACTIONBAR_PAGE = 4 (actions 37..48),
         RIGHT_ACTIONBAR_PAGE = 3 (actions 25..36). Geometry from ref-MultiActionBars.xml: a 38x500
         frame, button 1 at TOPRIGHT, each next TOP-to-BOTTOM of the previous at -6. -->

